  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#45712\", \"PowerToys#23857\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before. The Quick Access popup always opens in the bottom-right corner, even when the taskbar is on the left or top. PowerToys#45712 (Feb 2026, v0.97.2) asks for the popup to open next to the tray icon, either by auto-detecting the tray or through a setting that picks the corner. It is still open, and a commenter confirmed it with a taskbar moved to the top. PowerToys#23857 (2023) made the same request. I couldn't find a fix or a setting for it in the archive, so there is no workaround for now. Add a 👍 or your use case to #45712. Opening the popup with a global shortcut is the only alternative.\"}",
